<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    A leaf project rather than a Contracts/ folder: Humans.Consent and Humans.Users.Contracts
    reference this project, and Humans.Onboarding references Humans.Consent (the widget embeds
    Consent's signing step), so a folder inside Humans.Onboarding would close a project cycle
    (memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    ZERO ProjectReference, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING. Humans.Users.Contracts references this
    project for OnboardingResult, so a reference added here that leads back to Users.Contracts
    or anything that references it closes a cycle in a project nobody was looking at. If a type
    here ever needs something from another project, move the type out instead.
  -->

</Project>
